Tom: I did, but I felt a little sad. Some cages looked quite small.
Lucy: I know what you mean. But this zoo really focuses on the animals'' welfare.
Tom: Does it? How can you tell?
Lucy: They build each space to feel like the animal''s natural home, with plants and water.
Tom: That''s true. And the guide said they join many conservation projects.
Lucy: Yes. The money from our tickets helps protect endangered species in the wild.
Tom: Then I''m glad we came. Overall, a good zoo can be a caring place.', 'Lucy 问 Tom 是否喜欢今天的动物园之行;Tom 说喜欢,但看到有些笼子小有点难过;Lucy 说这家动物园很重视动物福利,会把每个空间打造得像自然栖息地;导游还说他们参与许多保护项目;门票的钱帮助保护野外濒危物种;Tom 觉得来对了,好的动物园是有爱的地方。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why did Tom feel a little sad at the zoo?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Some cages looked quite small.","The animals were too noisy.","The tickets were too cheap.","There were no animals to see."]},{"q":"How does this zoo show it cares about welfare?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It keeps all animals outdoors.","It builds spaces like the animals'' natural homes.","It lets animals go free every night.","It never feeds the animals."]},{"q":"What does the money from tickets help to do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Protect endangered species in the wild.","Buy new buildings only.","Pay the guides more.","Make the zoo bigger."]},{"q":"What did the guide say the zoo takes part in?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Sports competitions.","Many conservation projects.","Music shows.","Cooking classes."]},{"q":"What does Tom finally think about good zoos?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They are always cruel.","They should all close.","They can be caring places.","They are only for fun."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U2', 'sufe');
One big threat to them is illegal hunting.
When a species loses its safe habitat, it may slowly become extinct.
Protecting these animals is the reason why we set up national parks.
Every small action can help save a species from disappearing forever.', '世界上许多动物如今濒临灭绝;非法狩猎是它们面临的一大威胁;当一个物种失去安全栖息地,它可能慢慢灭绝;保护这些动物正是我们建立国家公园的原因;每一个小小的行动都能帮助一个物种免于永远消失。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is one big threat to endangered animals?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Too much food.","Heavy rain.","Bright lights.","Illegal hunting."]},{"q":"What may happen when a species loses its safe habitat?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It may slowly become extinct.","It grows much larger.","It moves into cities only.","It stops eating completely."]},{"q":"Why do people set up national parks?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To sell tickets.","To protect endangered animals.","To build new houses.","To go hunting safely."]},{"q":"What does the speaker say about small actions?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They are useless.","They cost too much.","They can help save a species.","They harm wildlife."]},{"q":"What is the main idea of the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Hunting is a good sport.","Zoos are boring places.","Animals do not need our help.","We should protect endangered animals."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U2', 'sufe');
Leo: I love animals too, Mia, but I''m a bit worried about feeding it.
Mia: Worried? Why? It''s cruel to leave a hungry cat with nothing.
Leo: If we always feed it here, more cats may gather and the yard could get dirty.
Mia: That''s a fair point. So what should we do instead?
Leo: Maybe we can call a local rescue centre to check its health.
Mia: Good idea. They could even find it a safe home.
Leo: Exactly. That way we are kind to the cat without causing new problems.', 'Mia 看到门口一只瘦猫想喂它;Leo 也爱动物但担心喂食;Mia 说让饿猫没东西吃太残忍;Leo 说总在这里喂会招来更多猫、院子会变脏;Mia 觉得有道理,问该怎么办;Leo 建议打电话给本地救助中心检查猫的健康,还能给它找个安全的家;这样既善待了猫又不会带来新问题。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Mia want to do for the cat?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Bring it some food.","Chase it away.","Sell it.","Ignore it."]},{"q":"Why is Leo worried about feeding it?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The food is too cheap.","More cats may gather and the yard could get dirty.","The cat dislikes him.","He has no time."]},{"q":"What does Leo suggest doing instead?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Keeping the cat in a cage.","Feeding it twice a day.","Calling a rescue centre to check its health.","Leaving the cat alone forever."]},{"q":"What could the rescue centre also do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Sell the cat abroad.","Teach the cat tricks.","Make the cat hunt.","Find it a safe home."]},{"q":"What do they finally agree is the best way?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To be kind without causing new problems.","To do nothing at all.","To feed every stray on campus.","To take the cat to a zoo."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U2', 'sufe');
Bats may sleep about twenty hours a day, but giraffes sleep less than two.
Some animals, such as bears, go into a deep sleep called hibernation.
They do this to survive the cold season when food is hard to find.
Each kind of animal has its own sleeping pattern.', '动物的睡眠方式各不相同;蝙蝠一天可能睡约二十小时,而长颈鹿睡不到两小时;有些动物,比如熊,会进入一种叫冬眠的深度睡眠;它们这样做是为了熬过食物难寻的寒冷季节;每一种动物都有自己的睡眠模式。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"About how long may bats sleep each day?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["About two hours.","About twenty hours.","About eight hours.","They never sleep."]},{"q":"How much do giraffes sleep, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["More than bats.","Exactly ten hours.","Less than two hours.","All day long."]},{"q":"What is the deep sleep of bears called?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Migration.","Hunting.","Conservation.","Hibernation."]},{"q":"Why do some animals hibernate?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To survive when food is hard to find.","To grow taller.","To play with others.","To travel far away."]},{"q":"What does each kind of animal have?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The same diet.","Its own sleeping pattern.","The same home.","No need for rest."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U2', 'sufe');
Anna: Yes, I do. It takes a lot of patience and a very gentle approach.
Ben: How do you start with a young dog?
Anna: We begin with one small, simple lesson and give a treat when it does well.
Ben: So you never frighten the dog?
Anna: Never. Fear only makes things worse. Kindness works far better.
Ben: How long does the whole training take?
Anna: It can take many months, but in the end the dog can guide a blind person safely.', 'Ben 问 Anna 是否帮忙训练导盲犬;Anna 说是的,这需要很多耐心和非常温和的方式;Ben 问怎么开始训练小狗;Anna 说从一个小而简单的动作开始,做得好就给奖励;她从不吓唬狗,恐惧只会更糟,善意效果好得多;整个训练可能要好几个月,但最后狗能安全地引导盲人。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does training a guide dog need most?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Loud noise and fear.","A lot of money only.","Patience and a gentle approach.","Many cages."]},{"q":"How does Anna start with a young dog?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["With a hard, long test.","By shouting at it.","By leaving it alone.","With one small, simple lesson and a treat."]},{"q":"What does Anna say about frightening the dog?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["She never does it.","It helps a lot.","It is sometimes needed.","It saves time."]},{"q":"How long can the whole training take?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A few minutes.","Many months.","One single day.","About one hour."]},{"q":"What can the dog finally do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Cook dinner.","Drive a car.","Guide a blind person safely.","Read a book."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U2', 'sufe');
Remember that every creature deserves kindness and respect.
Before you keep a pet, learn what kind of home and food it really needs.
If you find a hurt wild animal, call a rescue centre rather than touch it.
Small acts of care can build a more harmonious world for animals and people.', '给每一位爱动物的人一个小贴士:记住每个生命都值得被善待和尊重;在养宠物之前,先了解它真正需要什么样的家和食物;如果你发现一只受伤的野生动物,打电话给救助中心,而不要去触碰它;小小的关爱之举,能为动物和人类建立一个更和谐的世界。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who is this tip for?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only zookeepers.","Only scientists.","Only children.","Anyone who loves animals."]},{"q":"What does every creature deserve?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Kindness and respect.","To be ignored.","To be sold.","To be left hungry."]},{"q":"What should you learn before keeping a pet?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["How much it costs only.","What home and food it really needs.","Where to sell it.","How fast it can run."]},{"q":"What should you do if you find a hurt wild animal?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Pick it up at once.","Keep it as a pet.","Call a rescue centre.","Ignore it completely."]},{"q":"What can small acts of care build?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A bigger zoo.","A noisy city.","A larger cage.","A more harmonious world for animals and people."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U2', 'sufe');

